Subject: [VINUX-SUPPORT] New MarkupBinder beta version - 28 October 2010

> Hello all
>
> A new beta version of MarkupBinder is now available.  This version 
> features better support for writing single documents as an alternative to 
> a word processor, as follows:
>
> - Improved edit / review - with a single keystroke [Ctrl + 1] in gedit, 
> the document you edit in gedit is converted and displayed in Firefox.
>
> - The Build Document Page command converts your document to a stand-alone 
> HTML file, including an internal style sheet optimized for document 
> display, together with other required parameters.  As in the previous 
> version, the document can be converted to other formats for use in word 
> processors, for example, if you wish.
>
> - MarkupBinder uses the Markdown lightweight writing format and from this 
> version, you can reformat your Markdown document back to Pandoc Markdown 
> with the command md2mdp for a  polished and attractive appearance.
>
> MarkupBinder, as in previous versions, can create structured multi-file 
> documents that can be used as manuals, tutorial etc, for viewing locally 
> and on the internet.
>
> Thanks to Bill Cox for packaging MarkupBinder for Vinux and configuring it 
> for gedit.
>
> MarkupBinder is also available for Windows and installation from this 
> version is greatly simplified.
>
> The manual now contains an 'Installation' and a 'Getting started' section. 
> It is available locally by pressing [Ctrl + 7] in gedit or at:
> www.a-technic.net/MarkupBinder/docs/Manual
>
> To install (or update) in Vinux type:
> sudo apt-get update
> sudo apt-get install markup-binder
>
> Regards,
> Isaac
